# Claude Code credentials — NEVER commit.
#
# This repo is public, and ~/.claude is a symlink into it (~/.claude ->
# .dotfiles/.claude -> .claude-setup/.claude), so the live credential file the CLI
# writes lands inside this working tree. It holds the Anthropic OAuth token for the
# subscription login; committing it would publish an account credential, and `git
# add -A` from this directory was the only thing standing between that and a push.
#
# Never tracked in this repo's history as of 2026-11-03 — verified with
# `git log --all -- .claude/.credentials.json` (empty). Keep it that way.
#
# Both spellings are listed: the exact path the CLI uses today, and the bare
# filename so a future relocation (a per-profile or nested data dir) is still
# covered without anyone having to remember to come back here.
.claude/.credentials.json
.credentials.json
**/.credentials.json

# Claude Code session + runtime state — NEVER commit.
#
# Added 2026-11-12. Same reasoning as the credential block above, one class
# wider. ~/.claude is a symlink into this repo, so everything the CLI writes at
# runtime lands inside this working tree: full session transcripts, prompt
# history, pasted content, debug logs and file-edit backups. This repo is
# public. None of it has ever been committed — verified with
# `git log --all -- .claude/projects` (empty) — and the only thing standing
# between a transcript and a push was that nobody had run `git add -A` here yet.
#
# Transcripts are the sensitive one: they contain whatever was discussed,
# including file contents, tokens pasted into a prompt, and paths from private
# repositories.
.claude/projects/
.claude/sessions/
.claude/history.jsonl
.claude/paste-cache/
.claude/file-history/
.claude/shell-snapshots/
.claude/debug/
.claude/feedback/
.claude/backups/
.claude/todos/
.claude/state/
.claude/cache/
.claude/telemetry/
.claude/statsig/
.claude/stats-cache.json
.claude/.last-cleanup

# Editor/tool leftovers that accumulate in this tree
*.bak
.claude/settings.json.bak
